<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Mesoamerica and the Caribbean</p><h1 class="st-title">Centralist Republic of Mexico</h1><p class="st-meta">1835 CE – 1846 CE · capital Mexico City</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Mexico's conservative centralist state of 1835 to 1846, during which Texas broke away, France attacked Veracruz and war with the United States began.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 1835 a conservative congress backed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antonio-lopez-de-santa-anna">Antonio López de Santa Anna</a> abolished the federal system of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/first-mexican-republic">First Mexican Republic</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siete-leyes">Siete Leyes</a> of 1836 turned the states into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">departments</a> ruled from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico-city">Mexico City</a>, limited voting by property and created a Supreme Conservative Power to check the other branches.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Centralism provoked revolts across the north and south. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/texas">Texas</a> won independence at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-san-jacinto">San Jacinto</a> in 1836, Yucatán declared itself a separate republic in 1841, and federalists proclaimed the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/republic-of-the-rio-grande">Republic of the Rio Grande</a> in 1840. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> blockaded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/veracruz-city">Veracruz</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pastry-war">Pastry War</a> of 1838. Presidents changed often, among them <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anastasio-bustamante">Anastasio Bustamante</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antonio-lopez-de-santa-anna">Santa Anna</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mariano-paredes">Mariano Paredes</a>, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bases-organicas">Bases Orgánicas</a> of 1843 replaced the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siete-leyes">Siete Leyes</a>. The treasury was always near bankruptcy.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-states">United States</a> annexed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/texas">Texas</a> in 1845, and war broke out in 1846. In August 1846 a revolt restored the Constitution of 1824, creating the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/second-federal-republic-of-mexico">Second Federal Republic of Mexico</a> as the country faced invasion.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/centralist-republic-of-mexico.jpg" alt="Centralist Republic of Mexico" width="320" height="183"><figcaption>Image: Ludovicus Ferdinandus Can have elements by Sodacan and Heralder · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bandera_de_la_Rep%C3%BAblica_Central_Mexicana.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1835 CE – 1846 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Mexico City</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Anastasio Bustamante, Antonio López de Santa Anna, Mariano Paredes</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholicism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Spanish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/mexico">Mexico</a>, <a href="/countries/united-states">United States</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Mexican Republic (1835-1846)</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1840&amp;focus=centralist-republic-of-mexico" aria-label="Centralist Republic of Mexico on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="2001 1461 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Centralist Republic of Mexico lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M2321 1717L2321 1717M2321 1717L2464 1328M2321 1717L2321 1717M2321 1717L2590 1658M2321 1717L2386 1425M2321 1717L1937 1114"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M2321 1717h0M2464 1328h0M2321 1717h0M2590 1658h0M2386 1425h0M1937 1114h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M2321 1717h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M2321 1717h0"/></svg></a><figcaption